{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Defect\n\nEpic `6ed2-24e5-6985-4faa` (\"Merge held-out twin test modules after the code epics land\") closed on\nthe strength of an acceptance criterion that measured the wrong set. Its AC1 glob was:\n\n    git ls-files 'tests/**/test_*_heldout.py'\n\nwhich returns **0 rows** at `origin/main`. The epic was therefore reported complete.\n\nSix held-out modules are still in the tree. They are invisible to that glob because they end in\n`_heldout_<4-hex-quad>.py`, not `_heldout.py`:\n\n| created | LOC | tests | module | disposition |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026-08-06 | 137 | 8 | `tests/interfaces/facades/test_attestation_parity_heldout_2e16.py` | unpaired → rename |\n| 2026-08-06 | 75 | 4 | `tests/unit/metrics/test_dead_values_heldout_7504.py` | unpaired → rename |\n| 2026-08-06 | 122 | 9 | `tests/unit/test_reviewed_tree_binding_heldout_da31.py` | unpaired → rename |\n| 2026-08-06 | 145 | 9 | `tests/unit/test_snapshot_contract_heldout_8537.py` | unpaired → rename |\n| **2026-10-20** | 116 | 5 | `tests/unit/reconciler/mutate/test_update_priority_heldout_c9c6.py` | unpaired → rename |\n| 2026-08-06 | 176 | 10 | `tests/unit/test_code_review_provenance_heldout_2d1c.py` | **paired** → merge into `test_code_review_provenance.py` |\n\n45 test functions across 6 modules. Measured at `origin/main` from worktree\n`.rebar/worktrees/impl-e095` via `git ls-files --with-tree=origin/main | grep _heldout`,\n`git log --diff-filter=A --format=%ad --date=short -1 -- <path>`, and a per-module\n`git cat-file -e origin/main:<sibling>` existence check.\n\n**This is not a 771-LOC deletion.** Five of the six are unpaired, so their disposition is the\nrename `b721-6c6d-504e-45da` applied to the other 76 — drop the suffix, keep the tests. Only the\npaired module's 10 tests fold into an existing sibling. The value here is removing the last\nresidue of a retired convention and fixing the oracle that hid it, not LOC.\n\n## Why this matters beyond the residue\n\nThis is a **fail-open oracle applied to an acceptance criterion** — the same antipattern the\n`tests` code-review criterion flags in test code (`src/rebar/llm/reviewers/code-review-tests.md`),\noccurring in an AC, where no criterion looks for it. The AC's glob was narrower than the\nconvention it policed, so it passed by failing to see its subject. An AC that greps for a naming\nconvention inherits every gap in that convention's spelling.\n\nThe 2026-10-20 module is the load-bearing datum: it was added **after** the merge epic's stories\nwere created (2026-09-07), so this is not only residue — the convention is still being applied.\nThat recurrence is what story `d278-...` closes; this ticket removes what it already produced.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 — `git ls-files | grep -c '_heldout'` returns `0` at the change's HEAD.\n- [ ] AC2 — The 5 unpaired modules are renamed to drop the `_heldout_<quad>` suffix, keeping every\n      test function. `grep -c '^def test_'` per module is unchanged across the rename (8, 4, 9, 9,\n      5 respectively), recorded in a comment before the change lands.\n- [ ] AC3 — The 10 test functions in `test_code_review_provenance_heldout_2d1c.py` are merged into\n      `tests/unit/test_code_review_provenance.py`, whose `grep -c '^def test_'` increases by\n      exactly 10.\n- [ ] AC4 — No test function is deleted. Total collected test count at the change's HEAD is\n      greater than or equal to the count at its merge base, both recorded from\n      `pytest --collect-only -q | tail -1`.\n- [ ] AC5 — The detection expression this ticket's AC1 uses matches the `_heldout_<quad>` form,\n      demonstrated by running it against the pre-change tree and observing `6`.\n- [ ] AC6 — `make verify` is green at the change's HEAD.\n\n## Explicitly out of scope\n\nPreventing recurrence in the `rebar-implement` workflow. That is `d278-...`; this ticket removes\nthe residue, `d278` closes the vector. Do not add a gate here."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793650172900891450,"uuid":"904ab15e-6094-470b-b70f-60f252c1b69d"}